## 1. Using `Set` (The Modern & Easiest Way)

The `Set` object in JavaScript lets you store unique values of any type. This is the most concise and generally the most recommended method for removing duplicates.

**How it works:**
1. Create a `new Set()` from the array. This automatically filters out duplicates.
2. Convert the `Set` back into an array using the spread syntax (`...`).

**Example:**

```javascript
const arrayWithDuplicates = [1, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 1];

// 1. Create a Set to get unique values
const uniqueSet = new Set(arrayWithDuplicates);

// 2. Convert the Set back to an Array
const uniqueArray = [...uniqueSet];

